# =============================================================================
#  Media Countdowns — what should never be committed
#
#  Until V5 this repo tracked ~750 files under build/: object files, moc
#  output, clangd index shards and ninja logs. They churn on every single
#  compile, which buried real source changes in noise and made the history
#  far larger than it needed to be. Everything below is regenerated by
#  configuring and building, so none of it belongs in version control.
# =============================================================================

# Build output — any configuration, any generator
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
*_autogen/
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
.qtc_clangd/

# Qt / CMake generated sources
moc_*.cpp
moc_*.h
ui_*.h
qrc_*.cpp
*.moc

# Qt Creator per-user settings — machine-specific, differs per developer
*.user
*.user.*
.qtcreator/
CMakeLists.txt.user*

# Compiled objects and binaries
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.pdb
*.ilk

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# The public, keyless mirror of this source. Its own git repo, living inside
# this working tree — so it must be ignored here, or `git add -A` records it
# as a nested gitlink. That happened once already between these projects and
# had to be undone. It is published from its own folder, never from here.
Media Countdowns Public/

# The Windows Store edition. Its own git repo, living inside this working tree
# — so it must be ignored here, or `git add -A` records it as a nested gitlink.
# Same arrangement as the public mirror above. Store-only material belongs
# there, never here: this repo is the normal .exe edition and the shared source
# both editions build from.
Media Countdowns Windows Store/
